<title>POLAND: Poles change 5.2 mln NFI units to shares.</title>
<headline>Poles change 5.2 mln NFI units to shares.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poles have exchanged 5,204,730 units in Poland's National Investment Fund (NFI) mass privatisation scheme into shares of the 15 funds, the National Securities Depository (KDPW) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Poles have been eligible to exchange their unit into 15 shares, one in each fund, from May 12.</p>
<p>The funds entered the bourse's main market on June 12.</p>
<p>A KDPW official told Reuters that by Monday 15,778,960 million of the 25.6 million units purchased had been converted into book-entry form, a step necessary for bourse trade. @</p>
<p>Under the government's NFI programme, shares in about 500 mid-sized companies are allocated to the funds run by foreign and domestic management firms.</p>
<p>Each NFI has 31,026,185 shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
